hipfire is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE-APACHE).

Some individual source files remain under the MIT License (see
LICENSE-MIT), because their substantive authors have not elected
Apache-2.0 for their own contributions. Those files are identified by
their per-file `SPDX-License-Identifier` header, and their MIT grant is
preserved unchanged. MIT is compatible with, and freely combinable
into, an Apache-2.0 work; MIT's conditions are a strict subset of
Apache License 2.0 § 4.

Redistributing hipfire therefore requires satisfying Apache License
2.0 § 4 for the work as a whole — including shipping a readable copy of
NOTICE — and preserving the MIT copyright and permission notices on the
files that carry an MIT SPDX header.

See NOTICE for contributor attribution details, CONTRIBUTING.md for how
this applies to new contributions, and
docs/governance/relicense-2026-05.md for the full decision record.
